A student is asked to solve this. What value does this procedure return?
int[] a = {4, 3, 5, 1, 7, 3, -1, 7, 3};
int acc = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) if (a[i] > 6) acc++;
return acc;

This is a reasoning exercise. What does this string routine return?
String s = "ezayy";
int acc = 0, target = 'a';
for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) if (s.charAt(i) == target) acc++;
return acc;

At a staff meeting, an examiner notes the evidence: The case below gives the figures. Which index pair does this scan return?
int[] a = {3, 5, 6, 8, 10, 14, 15, 18, 22};
int i = 0, j = a.length - 1;
while (i < j) { int s = a[i] + a[j]; if (s == 16) return new int[]{i, j}; if (s < 16) i++; else j--; }
return new int[]{-1, -1};

In a problem set, an examiner notes the evidence: The case below gives the figures. What does this pointer code return?
Node a = new Node(20);
Node b = new Node(30);
Node c = new Node(5);
a.next = b; b.next = c; c.next = null;
Node p = a;
while (p.next != null) p = p.next;
return p.value;

On a work order, an examiner notes the evidence: The case below gives the figures. Consider the following question. Tracing this code:
int[] a = {4, 5, 9, 10, 14, 15, 17, 18, 22, 24};
int lo = 0, hi = a.length - 1, steps = 0;
while (lo <= hi) { int mid = (lo + hi) / 2; steps++; if (a[mid] == 27) return steps; if (a[mid] < 27) lo = mid + 1; else hi = mid - 1; }
return steps; Which answer is correct for this case?

On a schematic note, an examiner notes the evidence: The case below gives the figures. What value does this procedure return?
int[] a = {-2, 1, 5, 5, 0};
int acc = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) acc += a[i];
return acc;

In a sample analysis, an examiner notes the evidence: The case below gives the figures. Determine the value in question. What does this string routine return?
String s = "coxxcx";
StringBuilder out = new StringBuilder();
for (int i = s.length() - 1; i >= 0; i--) out.append(s.charAt(i));
return out.toString();

